1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Amalie Leontine Cahn Schwarzadler, was born in Frankfurt as the only daughter of four brothers: Siegmund Heinrich (1873-1890), Amalie Leontine (1875-1966), Robert Zacharias (1878-1948) and Arthur Isaak (1883-1952).
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT Her family of Jewish origin has been established in Frankfurt for many generations. Her history goes back to the "Schwarzer Adler" house on the Judengasse in Frankfurt ; His first ancestors are recorded as having been admitted to 
2 CONC the city of Frankfurt as early as 1505. His father was a consultant to the Chamber of Commerce and owner of a bank (Heinrich Cahn & Co.) which he ran successfully located on Taunusstrasse near the central station and the city's ma
2 CONC in banking district. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her mother was also a descendant of the extensive Goldschmidt branch of bankers and financiers.Present in the city since the  16th century . His younger brothers, Robert (Frankfurt am Main 1878-Barcelona 1948) and Arthur (Frankfur
2 CONC t am Main 1883-Santiago de Chile 1952), also established themselves as successful businessmen from a young age.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/pfdm?n=schwarzadler+goldsmichdt&oc=&p=leontine Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 23 2023, 16:53:28 UTC''
2 CONT
