3 CTRY England
1 TITL Maj. General
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Major-Gen. Joseph Lyon Barrow was born in Balham, London, on 11 February 1812. He was the son of Simon Barrow and Tryphina Esther de Symons. He married Alicia Egan, daughter of Colonel Kingston Egan, in 1847. He ma
2 CONC rried Emily McMaster. He died in 1890.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Major-Gen. Joseph Lyon Barrow was invested as a Companion, Order of the Bath (C.B.). He gained the rank of Major-General in the service of the Royal Artillery.
2 CONT
2 CONT At Addiscombe 1827-29, and a cadet in the Madras Artillery, he arrived in India on 25 January 1830, and was gazetted 1st Lieutenant on 1 September 1830; Lieutenant, 10 September 1848; Captain, 15 May 1851 ; Brevet Major, 28 Novemb
2 CONC er 1854;
2 CONT Lieutenant-Colonel, 18 February 1861; Colonel, 24 March 1865; Major-General, 1 August 1872.
2 CONT He was employed with General Wilson's force against Kurnaol in 1839; served with the China expedition from
2 CONT April 1840 to December 1843; and was at the attack on the heights of Canton, capture of Amoy, Chapoo,
2 CONT second capture of Chusan, Ningpo, heights of Segoan, Woosung, Shanghai, Chinkeangfoo, Nankin, and the
2 CONT whole of the operations in the Yangtse-Kiang River. 'No one better deserved his medal for China than Colonel
2 CONT (then Lieutenant) Barrow. It was at Chusan, we believe, that he distinguished himself, under the very eye of Lord
2 CONT Gough, by killing a powerful Mandarin in single combat' (extract from his obituary in Broad Arrow refers).
2 CONT He served in Central India in command of the Ordnance Department, Saugor Field Division. Mentioned in
2 CONT despatch of Brigadier-General H. Miller to the Assistant Adjutant-General, Saugor F.D., Camp Banda, 20 April
2 CONT 1858: 'It is not very often I believe, that opportunities offer to artillerymen of distinguishing themselves in any
2 CONT line other than their own, but some such, having presented themselves yesterday, were eagerly laid hold of by
2 CONT officers and men ... Major Barrow and Lieutenant Hennegan, gallantly supported by Lieutenant Blunt, of Her
2 CONT Majesty's 12th Royal Lancers, with a few of his men captured another gun'.
2 CONT Colonel Barrow was awarded the C.B. on 2 June 1869, and retired with the honorary rank of Major-General on
2 CONT 1 August 1872. 
2 CONT The Indian Mutiny Medal awarded to Colonel J. L. Barrow, C.B., Madras Artillery, who was mentioned for his
2 CONT gallantry in the First China War and in Central India, Indian Mutiny 1857-59, 1 clasp, Central India (Bt. Major J L Barrow. Ordce Dept. Saugor F Divn.)  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the elder brother of Captain Lousada Barrow of Barrow's Volunteer Cavalry. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Hamilton House, Southampton, on 29 October 1890, aged 83.
