1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *1873 - Link to '''[https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CS87-9Q91-P Death Record - Csenger, Hungary]'''
2 CONT *Rabbi Asher Anschel JUNGREISZ was also known as Anton and Antal Jungreisz in Hungarian Records. See his death record and this '''[https://bit.ly/2rGqHOX article]'''
2 CONT *Rabbi of Csenger for 40 Years. Author of ''Menuchat Asher'', published by his children posthumously. (Encyclopedia Judaica lists year of death as 1872)
2 CONT *Great great grandfather of married third cousins Esther & Theodore Jungreis.
2 CONT *See page 37, Shem Hagedolim Hasholaim L'Gedolei Hungariah, #203.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Yizkor - Csenger, Hungary: [https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/Csenger/cse017.html The Rabbonim of the Town]'''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?id=qAaUlkLC_lsC&pg=PA246&lpg=PA246&dq=Asher+Anshel+Halevi+Jungreis+family+tree&source=bl&ots=3m6QBNWZHP&sig=gxqHrAMv60S-kaz-PsPfLw3MGvs&hl=en&ei=Ibd9TO6iLsO88gax_cCCAg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&r
2 CONC esnum=6&ved=0CCoQ6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=Asher%20Anshel%20Halevi%20Jungreis%20family%20tree&f=false  '''Asher Anshel Family Tree]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Tshenger rov" Known by his famous book "Menuchat Asher"
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.ivelt.com/forum/viewtopic.php?f=31&t=6011&start=25   ''' ר' אשר אנשיל יונגרייז מטשענגער זצ"ל]
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://wiki.geni.com/index.php/Jewish_Dynasties '''Jewish Dynasties]
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT ר' אשר אנשיל יונגרייז אב"ד טשענגער בעמח"ס שו"ת מנוחת אשר - ה' כסלו תרל"ד
2 CONT
2 CONT נפלאות אשר : בו יסופר מכבוד קדושת אא"ז הרב ... מו"ה אשר אנטשיל שהי' אב"ד דק"ק טשענגער : מקצת נפלאותיו אשר פעל ישועות בקרב ישראל / הוצאתי לאור נכדו ישעי' הלוי יונגריז ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT JUNGREIS (Jungreisz), ASHER ANSHEL (1806–1872), Hungarian rabbi. Jungreis studied under Meir Eisenstadter and Jacob Koppel Altenkundstadt (Kunstadt) of Verbo, For 40 years he served as rabbi of Csenger and gained a widespread repu
2 CONC tation for his piety, to the extent that from all quarters people turned to him for amulets and cures from ailments. He supported widows, cared for the education and marriage of orphans, and also sent considerable sums to the Hung
2 CONC arian *kolel in Ereẓ Israel. After his death his children published his Menuḥat Asher in two parts (1876–1908), consisting of talmudic exposition and responsa. Jungreis left three sons who served in the rabbinates of various Hunga
2 CONC rian communities. ABRAHAM HA-LEVI (d. 1904) succeeded his father in Csenger. MOSES NATHAN NATA HA-LEVI (1832–1889) was rabbi of Fehergyarmat for 27 years, and of Tiszafüred for 21. He was the author of Torat Moshe Natan in two par
2 CONC ts (1896, 1923) and of Menuḥat Moshe (1905). SAMUEL ZE'EV HA-LEVI (d. 1909) was rabbi of Bojom for 30 years. His three sons-in-law were also rabbis: Joshua Baruch Reinitz (1823–1912), rabbi of Balkany and then Galszecs; Samuel Dav
2 CONC id Segal Jungreis (1837–1894), rabbi and rosh yeshivah of Fehergyarmat from 1868; and Jacob Schick (d. 1915), rabbi of Miskolcz and then of Nadudvar.
2 CONT
2 CONT BIBLIOGRAPHY:
2 CONT
2 CONT N. Ben-Menahem, Mi-Sifrut Yisrael be-Ungaryah (1958), 107f., 244f., 310f.; idem, in: Sinai, 61 (1967), 206; P.Z. Schwartz, Shem ha-Gedolim me-Ereẓ Hagar, 1 (1914), 17a no. 203; A. Stern, Meliẓei Esh al Ḥodshei Kislev Tevet (19622)
2 CONC , 14b no. 39.
