1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Oscar Emanuel Warburg (6 February 1876 - 1 July 1937) was a local politician.[1][2] The son of Frederic Warburg of London, he was educated at Trinity College Cambridge, graduating in 1898.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1909 he became a member of Paddington Borough Council,[3] In 1910 he was elected to the London County Council as a Municipal Reform Party councillor representing North Hackney. He remained a member of the council until a few mo
2 CONC nths before his death, becoming an alderman in 1931.[1] He served as Chairman of the London County Council in 1925 - 1926, during which term he was knighted "for political and public services".[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT During the First World War he served in the Royal Garrison Artillery, reaching the rank of captain.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Warburg was also a member of the Court of London University and an honorary freeman of the Metropolitan Borough of Hackney.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT An amateur botanist, with two taxon names [2]. 
