1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Helga Sjöbeck, f. Henriques
2 CONT Kunstner: Peter Most
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "... the story goes that Helga as you know was married to Pontus, and he was not a very wealthy man, and often had problems with money. In their family home in Sweden they had a painting of Helga's father, Vilhelm Moritz. They wer
2 CONC e having another financial situation and Helga decided to sell the painting to one of her brothers (I don't know which one, but apparently the one that was connected to the Henriques and Lovengren company - the o should have a lin
2 CONC e through it). In order for her husband to not lose face, she decided to make a copy of the painting herself. She was a talented artist and her husband never found out. Maybe you already know about the brother that was connected t
2 CONC o the Henriques and Lovengren company, it was a cloth factory? In fact it's the same company Magnus later worked for, the branch based in Malmo."
