1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charlotte Auguste Calmsohn was born on 23 August 1851. I J Weinberg’s memoir recounts that she married Nicolaus Falck who “became in the course of time a first-rate man of business …… He married my wife’s cousin Au
2 CONC guste Calmsohn and died a few years ago of heart disease, leaving a fortune of about £250,000”. Other sources spell the surname as Falk. The couple had a daughter, Caroline Anna Falk born in 1875
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Falk of Hamburg gave a silver and crystal fruit dish as a wedding gift as mentioned in the (Dundee) Evening Post of 14 September 1904 on the occasion of the wedding of Zeiline Adele Weinberg and Dr Curling Hayward. Auguste Fal
2 CONC k was a cousin of Agnes Weinberg née Simon, the bride’s mother. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolaus and Auguste Falk are both buried in the Jüdischer Friedhof Ohlsdorf Cemetery in Hamburg-Nord. Billiongraves.com has a photograph of their memorial gravestone in the Jüdischer Friedhof Ohlsdorf Cemetery in Hamburg-Nord:  ‘
2 CONC Nicolaus Falk, born 6 October 1836, died 31 December 1895. Auguste Falk née Calmsohn, born 23 August 1851, died 14 February 1932’. Findagrave.com also gives details. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also on the website jewishgen.org, Charlotte Auguste Falk née Calmsohn was born on 23 August 1851, died on 14 February 1932, and was buried on 18 February 1932 in an adjacent grave to her husband, plot B11 Nr. 232. Her address was
2 CONC  Mittleweg 51 and she was eighty.
