1 NAME Carl Jacob /Simon/
2 GIVN Carl Jacob
2 SURN Simon
2 _MARNM Simon
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 2 SEP 1850
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hamburg
3 STAE Hamburg
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 DEC 1924
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hamburg
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Photo of Carl Simon is from page 9 of the small publication "The House of May" (eight pages in all) written in 1949 to commemorate the hundredth anniversary of the firm founded by Carl's father Philipp Simon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Jacob Weinberg’s memoir gives the date of Carl's birth on page 20, and refers on page 123 to Carl working in his brother-in-law’s Isaac’s business in Dundee in December 1870. In the 1871 census record, Charles Simon from Ham
2 CONC burg was a twenty one year old clerk in a linen merchant’s office staying with his sister Agnes Weinberg at Fernbrae in Dundee, and this is almost certainly Carl. The Nottingham Evening Post’s account of the centenary of the lace 
2 CONC firm Simon May & Co on 24 September 1949 refers to Carl Simon as the founder’s son. 
2 CONT
2 CONT stolpersteine-hamburg.de The above website has a very long and detailed account about Carl Jacob Simon, his wife Rosa Gabrielle Seckels, and their descendants. Search on 'Erna Simon' who is their eldest daughter to read this accou
2 CONC nt
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Simon died on 7 December 1924. It was his wife Rosa Simon nee Seckels who died on 2 December 1933 according to their daughter Erna Simon's biography on stolpersteine-hamburg.de.     
