1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ida Lewisohn was from a well known family from Hamburg. She was married to great grandpa Wilhelm Hackenbroch in the 1870s and had five children, Josef, Leon, Max, Zerline and Fanny.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have a photo of her here in the USA and the original may be obtained from Mrs Ida Dunner c/o Schonfeld Square, London, UK.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a first cousin of "copper king" Adolph Lewisohn
2 CONT
2 CONT in New York, the railway magnate whose family built the Lewisohn Stadium at the start of the century.
2 CONT
2 CONT I am very occasionally in touch with a descendant of the same name here in New York.
