1 NAME Lazarus Baer /Mannheimer/
2 GIVN Lazarus Baer
2 _MARNM Mannheimer
2 NICK Ludwig
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 9 AUG 1806
2 PLAC Schopfloch, Bavaria, Germany
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 NOV 1864
2 ADDR
3 CITY Fellheim
3 STAE Bavaria
3 CTRY Germany
1 BURI
2 DATE 7 NOV 1864
2 PLAC Fellheim, Bavaria, Germany
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From birth records in Fellheim, Fran Luebke discovered that Ludwig was practicing medicine there by 1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludwig and his brother Moritz were both medical students at Ludwig Maximilians University in Munich.  This information was obtained via research done for us in Germany by Nancy Grossman. The translated text of the letter Nancy rec
2 CONC eived from the university is:
2 CONT
2 CONT Student registers from 1830/31 show that Ludwig and Moritz Mannheimer studied and lived together in Munich at “Am oberen Anger 885.” No registration can be found for the years 1831/32 as well as 1832/33. In 1833/34 Moritz Mannheim
2 CONC er (Schopfloch) is again found in the medical student registers with an apartment at Theaterstr. 8/1.  No registration is found for the 1834/35 school year.
2 CONT
2 CONT For Ludwig Mannheimer (Schopfloch) there is a Medical Diploma, No. 257, dated Apr. 5 1832.  His theme as “De venositate morbose aucta.”
2 CONT
2 CONT For Moritz Mannheimer (Schopfloch) there is a Medical Diploma, No. 378, dated Feb. 6 1834.  His theme was “De febre puerperali.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately, due to preservation measures it is not possible to provide copies of the documents.
2 CONT
2 CONT We hope to have helped you.
2 CONT
2 CONT Best regards,
2 CONT
2 CONT A. Mume
2 CONT
2 CONT End of translation.
2 CONT 5/31/99
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Lazarus Loew was actually an illegitimate grandchild of Ruben Kohn and Baerl’s.  I have no indication which of their children was the father or, more likely, the mother.  This information came from the same document that listed al
2 CONC l of Ruben’s children. (That document was probably from some census of the Jews.)
