1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Oscar Theodore Barrow was educated at Beaumaris Grammar School, Beaumaris, Anglesey, Wales. He was educated at Gloucester School, Gloucester, Gloucestershire, England. He entered the Indian Civil Service in 1875. H
2 CONC e was the Deputy Accountant-General in 1887 at Bombay, India. He was the Officiating Accountant-General and Deputy Commissioner, Paper Currency, Northwest Provinces in 1888. He held the office of Accountant-General for Bengal in 1
2 CONC 891. He held the office of Accountant-General for Bombay in 1894. He was invested as a Fellow in 1896 at Bombay University, Bombay, India. He held the office of Comptroller and Auditor-General for Calcutta between 1906 and 1911. H
2 CONC e was invested as a Companion, Order of the Star of India (C.S.I.) in 1907. He was invested as a Commander, Order of the British Empire (C.B.E.) in 1918.
